**Read:** Part II, The Book of Causation, SN 12–21 of [The Connected Discourses of the Buddha](../sources/Connected-discourses.lingua#r_1HH31B794G3FQFT1MWFCTXDD1Y), in sequence. Read the part’s introduction and complete its discourses; the highlighted themes below do not replace the remaining reading.

Return especially to the anthology’s passages in SN 12. Distinguish the conditions described in the text from a diagram you use to remember them. Keep the rest of this part in view rather than treating its first collection as the whole reading.

**Investigation:** Compare two formulations of arising or cessation. Record what changes, what remains, and whether an apparent contradiction concerns wording, scope, or interpretation. State which further passage could decide the issue.

**Carry forward:** keep SN numbers, translated terms, and your reason for choosing each comparison. Distinguish a discourse, its notes, and your reconstruction. Pause and revisit earlier reading when a term changes meaning in your account.

